ts they're not  walking down the street they're not  going to the phone book and looking for  their local restaurants they're going on  a digital platform to find out who  delivers for them the relationship  between humans and their local  restaurants are changing and has been  changing really ever since we started  this business one interesting direction  this could be heading is what's called  cloud kitchens these are basically  restaurants that only deliver there's  not even a storefront to walk into  Travis kalanick the founder of uber is  one of the big investors in this site  yeah my son uses this app or all three  of those apps like nobody's business  it just doesn't seem fair though that  they get that much out of the business  through the cut and it's not just with  restaurants right now we're seeing  pushback to something called class pass  which does this for fitness studios when  an app comes in and gets involved in  real-world business it can change a  whole business model I know when we did  a story on some of these apps and  restaurants scaling some of their menus  for it the one thing they did say is  they don't have to pay benefits to a  delivery driver they don't have to worry  about some of the other things that go  with it so when you look at that cut  while it's very high because you're  getting it from every restaurant for  some businesses there's that reason that  they want to also thanks Brooke

